Description: Linux system information viewer inspired by SIV64X
 SRS is a system information viewer for Linux that follows SIV64X, the System
 Information Viewer by Ray Hinchliffe (RH Software), built to improve on it and
 free for the Linux and open-source community. It is an independent project,
 not affiliated with SIV or its author, and contains no SIV code or data.
 .
 It provides a GTK 3 GUI (srs-gui) with 558 report items covering CPU,
 memory, sensors, storage, buses, GPU, network and the operating system, a
 CPU burn-in / stress tester, a GPU burn-in, Dhrystone/Whetstone,
 memory-latency, CPU, GPU and other benchmarks, a command-line report
 search (sysreport-search), a full text system report (srs-sysreport) and
 an optional root-only data collector
 (srs-root, run through pkexec or the srs-root@.service boot unit).
 .
 A built-in user guide (PDF and HTML, in /usr/share/doc/srs-sysinfo) explains
 every window, option and item; F1 or the Guide button in each panel opens it
 at that item's section.
